    "body": "Merge of main stopped (UMA), branch untouched at 64403d0d; PR left as a draft.\n\nMain's #1205 (6637e92c, `fix(sim): the hole-wall excuse measures a facet about its hole's axis`) rewrote the same check this PR changes, so the two fixes are incompatible, not just both-added:\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/swept.rs`: main deletes `chord_dip` and moves the excuse to the new `crates/sim/src/verify/hole_wall.rs::wall_excuse`. A facet is credited only if its sagitta about a declared hole axis (`HoleAxis`) is at most `WALL_SAG` = 0.05 mm, and then only min(sagitta, edge dip). Any other facet gets 0. This PR keeps `chord_dip`: full dip on declared-rim chords (`on_rim` / `HoleRim`), otherwise capped at `DEV_TOL` 0.01.\n- `solid_index.rs::hits`: main replaces the `hole_walls: bool` parameter with `walls: &[[f64; 2]]` (hole axes). This PR adds `hole_walls, rims`. `solid.rs`: main has `solid_hits_walled(.., &[HoleAxis])`, this PR has `solid_hits_rims(.., &[HoleRim])`. `generate.rs::contain_into`: main passes the holes as vertical axes, this PR passes the rim circles plus the drill's own radius. The same split shows in `contact.rs`, `rapids_posed.rs`, `mod.rs` and the `solid_law_goldens.rs` helper.\n\nBy arithmetic, main's #1205 already meets #1217's \"Done means\". An octagon on r 5 has a sagitta of about 0.38, and a 16-gon on r 5 about 0.096. Both are over 0.05, so they convict. A 96-gon is round and verifies clean. The 32-gon r 3 holes pinned here have a sagitta of about 0.0145, which is under 0.05, so no false gouges. I have not run this PR's `hole_wall_chord` cases against main.\n\nNeeds a maintainer decision:\n- (a) close #1228 as superseded by #1205 (after porting any `hole_wall_chord` case main lacks, as a test-only PR), or\n- (b) re-port the rim-only idea on top of `wall_excuse`. That would be a new design, not a conflict resolution.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
